-- Q242: Tax Procedures [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["1 year from the date the return was filed with the IRS","3 years from the later of the filing date or the return due date","5 years from the date the return was filed with the IRS","There is no statute of limitations on IRS assessments"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 6501(a), the IRS has three years from the later of the filing date or the due date to assess additional tax. Werner filed timely on April 15, 2024, so the IRS has until April 15, 2027. The period extends to six years under Section 6501(e) if the taxpayer omits more than 25% of gross income.
Wrong (A): One year is too short and is not a recognized assessment period under the Code.
Wrong (C): Five years is not the standard period. The general rule is three years, with a six-year extension for substantial omissions.
Wrong (D): A statute of limitations does exist for most returns. Only fraud or failure to file under Section 6501(c) removes the limitation period.$EXPL$
