Wrong (B): W-2 income with standard deductions closely matches statistical norms, producing low DIF scores. Self-employment returns with high deduction ratios trigger greater scrutiny.
Wrong (D): No income threshold exempts returns from DIF scoring. All returns are scored regardless of the amount reported.$EXPL$
