  choices = $EXPL$["Both gains are taxed at the same 20% rate because all long-term capital gains receive identical treatment","The collectible gain is taxed at a maximum 28% rate while the stock gain is taxed at 20%, costing $3,200 more in tax","The collectible gain is fully exempt from tax because collectibles held over one year qualify for a complete exclusion","The stock gain is taxed at 28% while the collectible gain is taxed at 15%, penalizing financial assets more heavily"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 1(h), collectibles (art, coins, stamps, gems) held more than one year are taxed at a maximum 28% capital gains rate, compared to 15%/20% for most long-term capital gains. Whitfield''s collectible gain of $40,000 produces $11,200 in tax (28%) versus $8,000 for the stock gain (20%), a $3,200 differential.
